From: Variscite PoC <noreply@variscite.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Allow flit_core 3 for the native Yocto build

Wrynose provides flit_core 3.12.0. Its build backend successfully builds
t61codec 1.0.1, but pyproject-build rejects the upstream <3 constraint
before invoking it. Permit Flit 3 without changing the package source.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 [build-system]
-requires = ["flit_core >=2,<3"]
+requires = ["flit_core >=2,<4"]
 build-backend = "flit_core.buildapi"
